 {'category':'authority_allocation','claim':'A backport question is followed by the author\'s preference and conditional deference to release-process participants. Instagibbs calls it a maintainer\'s decision; the author later expressly defers to maintainers over release timing. Dated contribution guidance assigns release and backport responsibilities to maintainers. A later participant report and metadata record a 30.x backport, but the packet does not show that the focal attribution caused that result or identify the individual decision-maker.', 'evidence':[ev('33453-014',bq['span']['quote']),ev('33453-017',br['span']['quote']),ev('33453-018',u7['span']['quote']),ev('33453-069',rback),*auth,ev('33453-086'),ev('M33473')],'unit_ids':['A013','A031','A032','A033','A034','A035'],'alternative_explanation':'The exchange may acknowledge an existing division of work while technical readiness and ordinary release scheduling account for the backport. The supplied report and metadata cannot identify its causal route.','status':'consistent_with'},
 {'category':'reason_giving','claim':'Pinheadmz defends open-source freedom to fork and choose software. Maluquices directly challenges whether that resolves the participation concern and asserts a transparency-and-diverse-input requirement. Pinheadmz then resists invoking open source here and asserts that the discussion has been open. This shows a dispute over application or premise of the principle, without verifying either side\'s empirical claims or establishing a new decision rule.', 'evidence':[ev('32406-227',before['span']['quote']),ev('32406-228',fresponse['span']['quote']),ev('32406-228',u13['span']['quote']),ev('32406-229',after['span']['quote'])],'unit_ids':['A019','A028','A029','A030'],'alternative_explanation':'The disagreement may concern what the public record already demonstrates rather than opposition to transparency or diverse participation as general values.','status':'supported_sequence'},
 {'category':'reason_giving','claim':'Jonatack quotes ajtowns\'s complete alternative treatment of deprecation and non-recommendation and explicitly agrees. This is an identifiable endorsement of a technical proposal, alongside a qualified Concept ACK, and is not itself recognition of an institutional duty.', 'evidence':[ev('32714-011',quote),ev('32714-013')],'unit_ids':['A022','A023','A024','A025'],'alternative_explanation':'The response can be read as conditional conceptual support for the current PR rather than commitment to one of the quoted alternatives; neither reading shows implementation.','status':'supported_sequence'},
 {'category':'scope_management','claim':'Darosior asks that conceptual discussion remain on a named mailing-list thread while offering a narrower output-count change and retaining support for #32359. The packet shows the request and bounded proposal, but supplies no specific response demonstrating compliance with the venue request.', 'evidence':[ev('32381-body',u9['span']['quote']),ev('32381-body',u10['span']['quote']),ev('32381-body','Notably this does not remove any command line option and keeps the limit in place on the size of each `OP_RETURN` output.'),ev('32381-body',u11['span']['quote'])],'unit_ids':['A015','A016','A017'],'alternative_explanation':'The routing may be an author preference for managing one PR rather than a recognized or enforced restriction on participation.','status':'unresolved'}
