# Complete screening: supporting scope is not a claim that content is intrinsically noninstitutional.
reasons={
 '32714-014':'Two local indirect editorial recommendations retained; the assertion that discouragement is deprecation is technical/semantic rationale rather than an institutional definition.',
 '32406-149':'Four distinct candidates: permission to defer minor changes, a persuasion expectation for fork accommodations, an external quoted technical preference, and a contrary practical preference not to switch PRs. ACKs, repeated quotations, predictions, and technical rationale are separately screened.',
 '33453-018':'Constitutive attribution of a specific release/backport decision and a separate personal plan not to object to either outcome.',
 '32381-body':'A discussion-routing request, the bounded technical output-count proposal, and an explicit recommendation for #32359; background, characterization, and hoped-for effects do not add independent candidates.',
 '32359-066':'One separate See navigation instruction. The external quotation and obfuscation reply describe technical consequences/capability, not institutional duties.',
 '32406-228':'One explicit normative transparency/diverse-input requirement. The other clauses give an argumentative response, asserted empirical rationale, and conjectured agreement; none independently verifies support.',
 '32406-148':'A concrete test assertion suggestion qualified by possible existing coverage, plus a conditional advisory documentation question. The intervening assessment is rationale; the unless question supplies scope rather than an additional prescription.',
 '32714-013':'No new statement: qualified Concept ACK, exact repeated quotation of 32714-011, and explicit agreement. The agreement is attributable endorsement, but the repeated proposal is not double counted.'}
